    "text": "1 day ago\nPremarket movers: SpaceX climbs, chip stocks rally, oil producers slump\nSpace Exploration Technologies Corp. shares rose 5% to $169.66, building on its 19% first-day rally.\nTech stocks across the board advanced, with Western Digital up over 5% and Micron Technology gaining 7%,.\nExxon Mobil shares fell 2% as Marathon Petroleum and Occidental Petroleum lost ground after the U.S. and Iran said they have reached a deal that will be signed on Friday. Delta Air Lines and United Airlines each rose 4% on the prospect of lower jet-fuel prices.",
